WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.891
Missing logs leave teams unable to reconstruct important events.

2
00:00:03.891 --> 00:00:15.615
Payment applications should capture authentication, authorization failures, administrative actions, sensitive data access, transaction changes, and configuration changes.

3
00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:20.135
Poor alerting creates noise without action or misses the events that matter most.

4
00:00:20.135 --> 00:00:29.235
Alerts should focus on suspicious behavior, high-risk changes, fraud indicators, and activity affecting the cardholder data environment.

5
00:00:29.235 --> 00:00:37.287
Delayed detection increases the time attackers have to abuse accounts, alter transactions, move laterally, or destroy evidence.

6
00:00:37.287 --> 00:00:40.410
Monitoring needs clear ownership and response paths.

7
00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:43.962
Insufficient monitoring can also harm assessment readiness.

8
00:00:43.962 --> 00:00:52.383
PCI DSS expects audit trails and review processes that support investigation, accountability, and security operations.

9
00:00:52.383 --> 00:00:56.763
Centralize application, identity, infrastructure, and cloud logs.

10
00:00:56.763 --> 00:01:00.795
Integrate security telemetry with SIEM or monitoring workflows.

11
00:01:00.795 --> 00:01:04.626
Review logs and alerts through documented, repeatable processes.

12
